WEBVTT

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.680
Konoha.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.680
This is my first arrest. I'm so nervous.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.980
Under arrest?

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.310
Touya Sagami.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.560
I am arresting you for a flagrant offense.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.020
Well, you have the right to remain silent

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.990
and the right
to retain a legal affairs AI.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.700
What are you doing?

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.030
Settle down!

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.450
Stop!
How are you allowed to arrest people?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.910
It's a flagrant offense--
a violation of Article 82.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.250
Never heard of it!

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.040
Bright!

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.920
Damn it. My breathing--

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.050
Why is it so cold?

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.760
An accident.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.390
That's right.
There was some kind of an accident.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:03.600
Hello? Mina?
Please pull yourself together.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.640
EPISODE 2: MIST AND DARKNESS

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.610
It's pitch black.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.400
Mina, are you hurt?

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.280
Are you okay?

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.570
Ouch.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.410
Are you okay?

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.250
Nasa. Nasa Houston.
Can you hear me?

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:26.250
-Houston?
-Houston?

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.670
Nasa.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.960
Nasa, are you okay?

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.710
-Are you hurt?
-I remember. She protected us.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.510
Oh, no! Well--

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.680
Nasa! Houston!

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.010
Oh, no.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.270
This is so bad. Is she dead?

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:48.560
She's breathing and has a heartbeat.
She is alive.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.440
Thank goodness.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.360
Nasa!

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.860
What should we do?

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.160
I'm requesting instructions from
the medical cloud, but cannot connect.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.030
No, call somebody. Maybe the police.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.620
The entire Internet is disconnected.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.750
Well, I don't really understand.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.380
But we'll be saved, won't we?

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.590
I don't know.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.470
No, no, no.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.390
OUT OF RANGE

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.760
Didn't they say it was safe?
That's why I came.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.600
What do we do?

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.230
Nasa!

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:29.980
I'm cold.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:31.940
My ears hurt.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.690
It's decompressing.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:38.700
If we don't hurry up and evacuate
to the shelter, we will suffocate and die.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.200
Shelter? Where is it?

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.580
Bright! Twelve!

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.920
Don't puke!
Don't you dare puke all over me!

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.210
Slow down your breathing.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.920
-Feeling better?
-Yes. I apologize.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:03.260
Okay.
Now it's about time you got off of me.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.760
Please don't get violent.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.930
The shelter should be nearby.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.230
Which way?

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.810
If we follow the wall, we'll get there.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:14.980
Got it.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:17.730
Ouch.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.150
-What's wrong?
-Nothing.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.120
It's not my fault.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.620
It's gravity's fault.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.290
The atmospheric pressure is dropping.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.210
There's a breach.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.340
We need to get away
before we run out of air.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.470
I don't think we'll run out of it
right away.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:44.680
We won't?

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.350
Mina, I am about to stop functioning.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:56.230
Soon,
this elevator will descend automatically.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.320
Don't give up. Go get helpâ€¦

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:00.990
Twelve.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.900
Twelve!

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.410
Excuse me.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.450
Operator.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.830
Hello?

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.830
Well, we're in trouble.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.380
No way.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.300
Anybody! Are there any adults around?

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.760
-Someone save us!
-Help!

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.930
It's dropping.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.430
It's okay.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.650
Twelve said
this elevator will descend automatically.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:37.150
Ouch.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:38.730
Nasa!

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.480
-Ouch.
-Thank goodness!

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.990
I don't think this was written
in the Seven Poem.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.410
The shelter.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:50.910
Which one?

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:52.870
This.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:56.670
Where?

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.040
It's cold. Hurry up and open it.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.420
Tell me in a way I can understand.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.510
You arrested the wrong person.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.970
-I'm requesting a legal affairs AI.
-What?

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.100
Restraint without the presence
of a legal affairs AI is prohibited.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.810
Bright is a legal affairs AI.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:18.560
Then call him. If he is not present,
I'll sue you for unlawful restraint.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.670
Isn't there a heater?

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.210
You should just be thankful for oxygen.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.760
I hate space. It's dark.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.180
Can't we make a call from this panel?

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:52.430
Not possible.
This shelter is incomplete as well.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.890
-Unbelievable.
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:59.900
There's some cold-protection gear
around here.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:01.860
Found it!

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.570
So warm!

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.910
What about for me?

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.870
There was only enough for one.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:13.450
That doesn't make sense.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.620
This place is under construction.
It hasn't been completely equipped.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:19.120
That's absurd!

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.460
That's because it went bankrupt once
and the management changed.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:25.170
-There have been delays.
-I'm coming in.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.630
-What are you doing?
-Emergency shelter.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.760
Stop! Don't pull on it.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.260
RESPECT OTHERS AND BE CONSIDERATE
IN THIS TIGHT SPACE

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.640
Ready, go.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.520
-It opened!
-Nasa!

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.810
Ouch.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.020
-It's so cold!
-I can't see anything.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.820
Let's huddle together.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.700
Follow along the wall.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.160
Where is the shelter?

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.660
Ouch!

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.950
Hiroshi, don't hold on so tight.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.660
-Idiot.
-This is why I hate kids.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.290
-Sorry.
-Sorry.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:04.670
Don't apologize.
I don't hate kids that much.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.380
KONOHA, ARE YOU SAFE? REPLY.
MESSAGE FAILED TO SEND

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.300
Ko-ko-ro-ha?

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:10.590
Don't look!

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:14.720
Koko-ha? Konoha? Which is it?

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.390
I said don't look!

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:21.640
If there's a breach,
does that mean we're gonna die?

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.110
This station has a stop-gap function
for patching breaches.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.610
YOU ARE IN THE A CYLINDER

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:29.070
But it might not be properly working.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.070
FULL MAP - A CYLINDER

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.280
Furthermore, during an accident like this,
the station is supposed to stop rotating.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.370
That doesn't work either.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.910
What are you trying to say?

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.080
-It could be terrorism.
-Yeah?

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.960
As a UN2 employee,
I can't overlook the possibility.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.920
What are you looking for?

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.090
There's supposed to be a printed manual
in the shelter.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.840
Placing your hopes on paper?

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:56.350
This is bad. The air is getting thinner.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.140
Here it is.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:00.850
Where?

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:03.310
There's a manual.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.360
Nasa!

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.320
Nasa! Don't die yet!

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.190
No, this is awful!

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.280
I can see her breath. She's alive.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:16.030
Nasa! Where is the shelter?

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.410
Nasa! Wake up!

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.410
This might be it.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.580
All we can do is sit still and wait.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.880
No, we'll escape. We have to move.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:33.010
We Japanese don't get frantic and agitated
in situations like this.

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:34.930
The opposite is true in zombie movies.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.640
The guys who sit still die.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.890
Zombies are irrelevant right now.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.770
I hate zombie movies.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.690
They only ever have tyrannical characters
like you in them.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:47.690
-You're scared of zombies.
-What?

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:51.400
What are you saying?
I'm not afraid of them.

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:56.320
You haven't adapted to Mars gravity yet,
have you?

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:57.820
What?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:00.830
You skipped your gravity PT appointments,
didn't you?

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.830
That's why you collapsed before.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.580
Shut up.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:08.580
Much better than spinning around
in zero gravity like you.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:13.090
You're the one who can't live on Earth
because of your weak condition.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:16.300
As if I want to go to Earth.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:20.760
The Japanese government is planning on
cutting back manned missions next year.

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:21.760
What?

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:25.520
We got an administration that is reducing
the science and technology budget.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:26.730
So?

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:30.230
You keep yourself locked up in space
and won't come down to Earth.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.570
It's hard on our government.

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:34.860
I don't know if you understand.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.700
You are a nuisance.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:43.950
Living and having kids in space
isn't right for humans to begin with.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.620
Are you saying I should die?

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.290
No.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.090
It's just that there are a lot of people
saying that stuff.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.300
Ouch!

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:55.880
Ouch! What are you doing? Stop!

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:58.010
I saved you.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.760
I hate Earthers.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.640
You should all get blown into extinction
by a meteorite.

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.560
You're a follower of John Doe, aren't you?

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:09.940
What?

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.770
Your drone hacked the system.

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:15.530
Then I discovered
a cognitive-limiter violation.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.650
Right after that, this accident occurred.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.740
You don't know who you're talking to.

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:22.070
I'm just tolerating you now,

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:25.160
but I could report you
for suspicion of terrorism.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.200
That's ridiculous.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:30.670
Then why would you unlock
your cognitive limiter?

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:34.420
-None of your business.
-Yes, it is! Explain yourself!

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:37.380
I'm going to exterminate all you Earthers

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:40.220
by raising a Lunatic that surpasses Seven!

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.300
Happy now?

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:46.770
How long was I unconscious?

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:48.180
About ten minutes.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:49.770
Ouch!

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.560
I'm so embarrassed.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.690
Don't look, you brat.

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.020
Ouch!

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:59.070
-What about painkillers?
-They're the drowsy type, aren't they?

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.570
We need to get to the shuttle.
We could get left behind.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:06.580
-If only we stopped rotating.
-What do you mean?

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.920
Normally when an accident occurs,
the active brakes will activate

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.130
and zero gravity will occur.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:16.250
If that happened,
we could float up to the top.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.050
Is that so?

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:21.720
Was there an ONIQLO
in any of the boxes under the floor?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:25.260
-ONIQLO?
-Oh, you mean an ONIQLO suit.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.850
It is a simple space suit,
just like the shuttle suits.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:30.980
According to the manual,
it should be around here.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:34.650
So if we can make it outside in that,
we can go home to Earth?

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:38.280
It's cheap and vinyl.
You wouldn't be able to go out in it.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.490
Vinyl?

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:42.490
-However, it's better than nothing.
-Found it!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.410
There aren't any.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:48.200
If we had ONIQLOs,
we could survive the cold and radiation.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:50.000
They left them out?

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.000
Oxygen!

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.210
What have you been up to?

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.920
There's no Internet connection.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.220
-Peer-to-peer?
-Don't look!

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:06.640
I'm wearing an ONIQLO now. It's warm.

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:08.890
The gloves are Smart-equipped.

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:11.140
It's too loose for me.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.230
If I could do a live feed of this,

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:17.310
I might get 100 million followers.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.900
If only I could at least
get the landscape outside in a selfie.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:22.900
Oh, yeah. Peer-to-peer.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:25.450
Is peer-to-peer Internet?

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:27.780
There has been no connection for awhile.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.830
Peer-to-peer isn't Internet.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.500
Peer-to-peer
connects devices to each other.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:36.880
By pairing devices,
you can get up to 200 meters--

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.170
Found it!

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:41.920
Oh, a peer comm?

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:44.930
Like when you connect handcuffs
or a drone--

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.800
Are you trying to boot up
that illegal drone?

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:50.180
-I won't let you!
-Get off me!

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:54.520
I'll boot up Bright first
and shut your drone down.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.310
I win!

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.020
How childish.

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:00.940
I have an image.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.690
This is-- The spa hub is directly below.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.410
Bright has paired now too.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.030
Bright. Get up.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.620
Explore the area.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:15.710
There are containers. ONIQLO--

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.460
Found them. ONIQLO suits.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:21.840
But the atmospheric pressure outside
is about the same as on Mt. Fuji's summit.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:22.920
KONOHA, REPLY.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:26.300
With our current equipment,
it would be very-- Touya?

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:29.050
You're going?

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:30.470
That's absurd.

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:32.220
Let's wait here for help.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.890
I won't allow you to go out there alone.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:36.980
It's cold!

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:40.480
Got it. Selfie connected.

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:42.980
Selfie, turn on your high-intensity light.

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:44.070
EARTH GRAVITY FLOOR

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:46.110
I can see. I wonder if there's air.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.240
AIR PRESSURE - TEMPERATURE

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:50.200
Why can't he close the door?

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:53.790
It's cold.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.960
There it is. An ONIQLO suit.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:00.380
Okay, I think it's feet in from the top.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:02.500
All right, got it on.

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:05.710
Quickly.
Let's climb up and get on the shuttle.

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.300
Come on, Dakky.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:11.640
Wait a minute. Where are you going?

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:12.890
Bright.

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:14.850
Why are you going down?

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:16.480
None of your business.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:18.810
Dakky, light.

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:32.830
-I'm not letting you get away.
-I'm not running away.

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:53.600
You're trying to get to that girl Konoha,
aren't you?

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.260
What is this?

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:58.770
It looks like a disposable mask.
Nonwoven fabric?

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:01.770
A light bulkhead. Made out of fabric.

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:05.400
A bulkhead? How are you so well-versed?

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.490
This can be manually opened?

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:14.780
When the air pressure
on both sides is the same.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:16.540
Bright.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.080
Don't follow me.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.920
I can't leave you. I'll accompany you.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:27.920
You said you were going to raise Lunatic
and destroy everybody on Earth.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.050
So what?

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:32.180
You have no idea how horrible Lunatic is.

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.180
Shut up, Earther.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:37.310
You people will never understand me.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:38.600
Not ever.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:42.350
Well, well. You trying to compete?
I won't be beat this time.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:48.440
Do you think a PT dropout like you
can beat an Earther who lives at 1G?

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.780
Go extinct, Earther!

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.540
He's so slow.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.630
What's that sound?

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:15.800
Maybe I should go back for him.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.150
Hang on a second!

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:31.240
The interior contractors shouldn't be
loading materials in a place like this.

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:35.610
Wait!

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:39.620
Look out!

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:43.120
A fabric bulkhead?

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:45.790
-Why is it inflated in the back?
-Don't touch it!

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:48.500
Behind this, it is a vacuum.

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:50.960
Touch it and it's curtains for you.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:53.510
Here.

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.930
Thank goodness
it's on this side of the bulkhead.

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:57.010
KONOHA BAIKONUR NANASE

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:01.770
Nobody's here.

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.320
Konoha!

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:20.120
Are you okay, Konoha?

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:22.410
Oxygen deficiency.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.910
What's the matter? Is she dead?

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.170
We need to hurry up
and take lifesaving measures.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:32.460
Damn it. The password.

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:38.300
-What are you doing?
-Lifesaving actions.

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:40.760
-Are you breaking the law again?
-Shut up!

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:45.600
If I followed the laws made
by Earther AIs, we'd both be dead.

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:47.100
Don't interfere!

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:51.520
Her breathing's stopped.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:53.070
The password.

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:56.150
Damn it!

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:58.240
What are you doing? Out of the way!

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:00.410
Excuse me.

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:05.750
A password Nasa might use--

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:07.410
Maybe--

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.580
PLEASE ENTER PASSWORD

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:11.670
Yes.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:13.750
Cardiopulmonary.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:15.050
Here it is.

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:19.720
She's revived.

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.300
Konoha, hold on.

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:32.520
Implants?

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:35.480
The rumors were true then?

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:36.570
Yeah.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.570
We have implants in our brains.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:44.660
It was originally
just to adjust the balance of hormones.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.790
But it can also access reflex,
cardiopulmonary

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:48.830
and other important functions.

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:54.550
Of the 15 moon-born,
ten died by age three.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:58.720
They found out that the low gravity
on the moon's surface

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:01.050
has a fatal impact on growing infants.

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:04.180
The surviving five children
had implants embedded.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.850
Moon child syndrome.

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:09.730
They worked well in infancy.

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:12.230
But it was uncertain what would happen
in the second period of growth

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:13.940
when the hormone balance changes.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:15.770
Nobody knew.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:17.940
So before that,

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:21.820
the implants were supposed to dissolve
and break down into water and nitrogen

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:23.370
per the design.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:26.830
Due to a design flaw,
they didn't dissolve?

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:28.080
They started to dissolve,

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.790
but with the design flaw,
half of the implant remains.

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:33.130
I still have time with mine,

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:36.040
but Konoha's is out of time.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:39.260
We have to prosecute the firm
that made them.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:43.760
The firm that designed them went bankrupt.
There's nobody to sue.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:46.140
Is that firm--

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:48.520
Seven Technology.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.100
Seven designed them?

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:54.940
Yes. It is a product
from its period of peak intelligence.

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:57.070
Lunatic Seven.

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:59.690
But Seven's intelligence collapsed.

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:01.450
It was euthanized.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:04.780
So now nobody understands
the design philosophy itself,

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.530
much less the design flaws.

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.870
No human, no AI.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:10.620
Are you--

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:12.460
That's why the Lunatic is so--

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.710
Found them!

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:16.340
It's me. Mina.

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:19.840
-It's too bright.
-Sorry about that.

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:21.800
Touya, it's me.

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:23.550
Nasa.

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:26.430
Nasa is too weak
to make it to the top.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:28.930
She said to bring a wheelchair.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:38.070
Where is this?

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.870
It's been a long time.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.420
Touya! Taiyou!

00:20:58.590 --> 00:20:59.630
Hakase.

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:02.050
Nasa.

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:06.050
Touya, are you okay? Ouch.

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:07.840
Is everyone all right?

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:12.560
I've hurt a rib. But never mind that.
How is Konoha?

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:16.100
Is she another moon-born kid?

00:21:16.190 --> 00:21:17.940
Yeah, probably.

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:20.400
She lived in Tateana City on the moon.

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:21.570
Tateana City?

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:24.820
A Japanese moon-surface city
in Marius Hills.

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:29.070
She might be easier to talk to.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:30.700
She stopped breathing?

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:34.080
I restored it immediately. It's fine.

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:37.710
Touya, you didn't hack
the implant again, did you?

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:38.960
Why not?

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.300
That isn't something
you can carelessly fiddle with.

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.710
-If you made even one mistake--
-Nasa.

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:45.880
He saved her life.

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:49.720
If he hadn't done that,
Konoha would be dead right now.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:51.510
I know.

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:53.470
I wasn't carelessly fiddling with it.

00:21:54.350 --> 00:21:56.730
I've experimented on my own implant
in the lab many times.

00:21:57.480 --> 00:22:00.400
I know that, but don't do it anymore.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:03.690
Konoha's implant
is in worse shape than--

00:22:03.780 --> 00:22:04.990
I knew it.

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:09.870
Wasn't it you and my uncle
who laughed it off as an urban legend?

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:11.910
Touya, there's a good reason that--

00:22:11.990 --> 00:22:15.870
You adults were in on it
and kept it from us all this time.

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:20.210
Nasa.

00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:23.460
Did I faint again?

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:25.630
Yes, but it's okay.

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:28.130
It's not your fault.

00:22:28.970 --> 00:22:30.140
The implants.

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:31.890
You were listening?

00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:35.470
Right, Touya?

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:40.650
I want to get better soon
and then go to Earth.

00:22:43.110 --> 00:22:46.320
Konoha, you'll be able to go to Earth
after just a bit.

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:48.400
-Good luck.
-Thank you.

00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:50.410
We're going up again?

00:22:50.490 --> 00:22:54.280
Why did that elevator go
all the way to the bottom?

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:57.580
It's for safety.
It would be dangerous if it fell.

00:22:57.660 --> 00:22:59.960
They really have no regard
for their guests.

00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:01.830
I'm gonna sue once we've been saved.

00:23:01.920 --> 00:23:05.500
Everybody, please stop with
the idle chatter and keep walking.

00:23:05.590 --> 00:23:09.170
If we can get to the shuttle area,
we can probably get on a rescue ship.

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:12.840
Taiyou has been pretty full of himself
for quite some time, hasn't he?

00:23:12.930 --> 00:23:15.720
I'm a temporary employee of the UN2,

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:18.600
so I have a duty
to rescue everybody in a disaster.

00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:21.270
-UN2?
-The UN2?

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:23.520
-What's that?
-The United Nations!

00:23:23.610 --> 00:23:25.730
You're not an employee.
You're a nonregular.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:27.320
It's like a part-time job.

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:29.610
Taiyou.

00:23:29.690 --> 00:23:30.860
Yes?

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:34.280
Sorry for any trouble
Touya's caused you.

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:37.330
He can be sharp tongued,
but he really is a good person.

00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:39.410
Yes. You're right.

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:41.080
He is sharp tongued, isn't he?

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:42.870
I'm sorry for the trouble.

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:45.090
Stop doing that right in front of me!

00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:47.590
What's this, a balloon?

00:23:48.170 --> 00:23:50.010
A balloon bulkhead.

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:52.510
We came from the other side of it.

00:23:55.350 --> 00:23:57.010
It automatically repairs itself.

00:23:57.100 --> 00:23:59.020
Seems like
there is oxygen on the other side.

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:00.730
A spa?

00:24:00.810 --> 00:24:03.900
This says it is a super-bathhouse--
"Anshin Springs."

00:24:03.980 --> 00:24:06.360
I guess that's why
this is called a spa hub.

00:24:06.440 --> 00:24:08.780
It says you can see Earth from the bath.

00:24:08.860 --> 00:24:12.490
This is the Mars floor.
So it must be 100 meters more.

00:24:13.280 --> 00:24:15.820
Something like a 30-story skyscraper.

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:20.160
As we climb higher, there's less gravity,
so it'll be easier than lower down.

00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:22.120
Konoha.

00:24:22.750 --> 00:24:26.040
I'm Mina. From Saitama on Earth.

00:24:26.130 --> 00:24:30.170
Both you and Touya were born
on the moon, right?

00:24:30.260 --> 00:24:34.260
We were raised together in Tateana City,
a city on the moon's surface.

00:24:34.340 --> 00:24:38.100
Even so, your personalities
are like night and day, aren't they?

00:24:39.390 --> 00:24:42.140
Konoha,
how many followers do you have?

00:24:42.230 --> 00:24:44.100
I don't use SNS.

00:24:44.190 --> 00:24:46.730
Really?
I didn't know people like you existed.

00:24:46.810 --> 00:24:47.900
Wow!

00:24:47.980 --> 00:24:51.230
Could you please do that later? Let's go.

00:24:54.400 --> 00:24:56.530
Just one more.

00:24:56.620 --> 00:24:58.410
Are you excited to see your parents?

00:24:58.490 --> 00:25:00.040
-Mina.
-What?

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:02.950
-You shouldn't ask about her parents.
-Why not?

00:25:03.540 --> 00:25:07.710
I think Konoha's father died
in an accident on the moon's surface.

00:25:08.290 --> 00:25:10.380
And Touya's parents too.

00:25:11.050 --> 00:25:13.720
I mean, it happened years ago.

00:25:14.340 --> 00:25:16.300
What kind of accident was it?

00:25:19.800 --> 00:25:21.310
I'm not sure.

00:25:21.390 --> 00:25:25.440
Internet rumors say they were doing
some kind of an experiment.

00:25:29.150 --> 00:25:31.980
All right. We just need to climb up here.

00:25:40.740 --> 00:25:41.740
Konoha.

00:25:44.080 --> 00:25:46.000
Konoha, what's wrong?

00:25:47.250 --> 00:25:48.250
The snow--

00:25:51.130 --> 00:25:52.500
It's snowing.

00:25:52.590 --> 00:25:53.710
Snow?

00:25:57.220 --> 00:26:00.300
There's something at the top.

00:26:00.390 --> 00:26:04.140
-Stop the wheelchair!
-What? Did something happen?

00:26:05.060 --> 00:26:08.900
There's snow falling in the station.

00:26:09.560 --> 00:26:12.650
Oxygen-- The oxygen is escaping.

00:26:19.410 --> 00:26:20.410
Run!

00:26:20.490 --> 00:26:23.030
What's happening up there?

00:26:23.120 --> 00:26:24.200
Run!

00:26:25.830 --> 00:26:27.160
Run!

00:26:32.920 --> 00:26:34.750
Hurry up and close it.

00:26:51.270 --> 00:26:52.360
What is this?

00:26:52.940 --> 00:26:54.320
Do what I do.

00:26:54.400 --> 00:26:56.320
First, pull the handles.

00:26:56.400 --> 00:26:58.700
Bring out your hoods and gloves.

00:26:58.780 --> 00:27:00.280
Fasten everything tight.

00:27:00.990 --> 00:27:03.740
Once everything is fastened and locked,
release the valve.

00:27:05.410 --> 00:27:07.200
Nasa and I are all suited up.

00:27:08.120 --> 00:27:09.620
My fastener.

00:27:11.460 --> 00:27:13.880
Damn it! It's not catching.

00:27:15.920 --> 00:27:18.090
Here is some oxygen. Can you hear me?

00:27:18.170 --> 00:27:19.630
Breathe in the oxygen.

00:27:20.380 --> 00:27:22.050
What is that? Something is here!

00:27:22.140 --> 00:27:25.100
Oh, no. She's hallucinating
from oxygen deficiency.

00:27:25.640 --> 00:27:28.060
There it is!

00:27:33.520 --> 00:27:36.730
I am Anshin-kun, the station fairy.

00:27:36.820 --> 00:27:39.190
-Chief.
-Chief?

00:27:40.450 --> 00:27:41.990
The rift is getting wider.

00:27:48.540 --> 00:27:50.830
Follow this guy.

00:28:10.390 --> 00:28:11.850
Oops.

00:28:12.890 --> 00:28:14.060
Jump!

00:28:19.150 --> 00:28:20.190
I can't--

00:28:21.280 --> 00:28:22.950
I can't reach it.

00:29:54.660 --> 00:29:58.080
Subtitle translation by:
Noelle Marie Hollister
